WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.601
I'm here with my co-host,
Jack Harlow!

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:08.667
Now, since you're starring
in the upcoming remake

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.434
of "White Men Can't Jump,"

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:12.267
I thought I'd put
your skills to the test

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:15.200
in a "Random Object Shootout,"
okay?

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.567
Are you gonna kill me at this?
-We'll see.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.634
-Yeah, yeah.
-I feel good.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:19.968
-Yeah.
Here's how this works.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.934
We're gonna take turns
trying to shoot random objects

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.501
into that hoop behind us.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.000
If you make it in,
you get a point.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.200
Let's see
what our first object is.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.267
It is...

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:30.968
♪♪

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:33.834
...a jack-o-lantern.
Okay.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:34.968
-Who's shooting first?

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:39.167
-Uh, well, you're my guest,
so maybe...

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.934
You want me to go first?
-It has some weight to it.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.701
-Yeah, I know.
It's got a little heft.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.133
You can --
You can toss it like that.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.567
-But I can let it fly.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.701
You don't care about
what happens, anything?

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:48.868
-Well, as long as it's
towards the hoop, yeah, yeah.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:49.868
-That's what I mean.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:52.567
-I want the audience to be safe.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.767
-This is the spot?
-Yeah, that's --

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:58.267
Well, you can go up here.
You can go up here.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.701
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.267
Smashed the pumpkin.
All right now --

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.834
-All right, bend your knees.
Bend your knees.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:04.467
-All right.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:08.968
♪♪

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:12.200
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.567
-Come on.
-Thank you for the tip.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:17.467
All right.
Let's see the second object.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:21.033
Cornucopia full of eyeballs.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.367
Here we go.
Now, I think, for this,

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.000
you actually have
to get the cornucopia,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.100
the basket, in the basket,
really.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.200
Don't worry about the eyeballs
so much.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.567
That's just spooky
for spooky season.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.701
-By all means.
-Really?

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:33.968
-By all means.
-That's so nice.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.734
Thank you, bud.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:40.801
♪♪

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:43.133
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.300
Sad?
-It's all right.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.000
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.167
-You were so disappointed in me
right there.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:52.667
♪♪

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.734
Oh!

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.234
♪♪

00:01:57.234 --> 00:02:00.501
That's skill!
That's skill right there!

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:03.934
That's skills.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.501
All right.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.067
The third object --
-Hold on.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.334
-That stays in there.
That's good.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:09.701
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:13.534
Third object is...

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.567
a vase full of applesauce.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:16.834
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.267
It's apple-picking season.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:21.133
You can do a bunch of
different things with apples.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.234
Applesauce is one of them.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:26.467
♪♪

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:28.834
You ready?
-Who's first?

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.033
-I think you should go first.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.801
You're the one
who sank the basket.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.567
♪♪

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.033
Just be careful.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.501
Be care-- Don't worry.
-I don't want this on me.

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:41.100
-It won't hurt anybody.
Yeah.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Come on!

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.467
What?!

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:46.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:49.367
Can we see that again?

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:50.834
Whoa!
Swish!

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.601
-And my cornucopia
is still in there.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.934
-Exactly!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.033
Dude.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:00.167
Oh, my gosh.
All right.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:03.067
♪♪

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.534
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:10.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.467
All right...
-What a mess.

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.033
-Clean up is gonna be tough.
It's all right.

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:15.968
We're gonna be all right.
-I'm sure you won't be involved.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.901
-We're going to be --
I'll help out.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:21.100
Don't go anywhere near there,
all right?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.934
All right.
I had some extra muscle --

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:25.667
All right, here we go.
This one right here, this is...

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.167
Oh, this is Necco wafers.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:30.234
This is something that Jack --
-Are they edible?

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.868
-Yeah, they're candy --
famous candies

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:35.167
that no kid wants to get
on Halloween.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.267
So, we got all the Halloween --
we're gonna do it now.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:39.834
How's it taste?

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.167
-Good.
-Yeah, right.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.534
All right, ready for this?
-Middle-of-the-road candy.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.467
-Thank you.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:48.868
Necco wafers, here we go.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.200
-Whoo!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.567
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.434
-Someone gave me a "whoo."

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:58.901
Someone threw me off
with their "whoo."

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:01.067
Someone said, "Whoo!"

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:04.267
All right, bud.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.467
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Sad tuba ]

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.834
-It's the cheers.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:11.000
-It looks actually pretty good
with my applesauce splatter.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.267
Actually looks kind of festive
and gorgeous.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.434
All right.

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:16.767
Now, look, guys,
it is time for the moneyball.

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:19.300
-Imagine what's in here.
-This is worth --

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.501
This is worth 5 points,

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.434
so whoever sinks this wins,
okay?

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:25.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:28.000
It is a Mike Myers...
-That ain't right.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.133
-Jack, you go first.
Good luck.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.534
♪♪

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:35.300
It's a Michael Myers head
from "Halloween."

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.968
-This is actually --
-Not bad?

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:39.067
You think you can do it?

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:41.801
♪♪

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:49.567
♪♪

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.567
-Ah.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.200
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.868
♪♪

00:04:56.868 --> 00:04:58.901
I mean,
are you kidding me, man?

00:04:58.901 --> 00:04:59.934
You know what?
I gotta be honest --

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.100
-I got all my [bleep] in there.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.234
[ Laughter ]
Everything I own.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.267
I'm gonna throw my phone
in there.

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.567
-No, don't throw your phone
in there.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:07.167
Oh, my --
You know what?

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:08.834
I hurt my wrist a little bit
on that last one.

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:10.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.434
-You want me to shoot yours?

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.200
-No, I think I'm gonna have
someone else take my shot.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.467
Please welcome three-time NBA
champion and executive producer

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.934
of the new Netflix documentary
"The Redeem Team,"

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.300
Dwyane Wade, right there.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:23.501
-Yo,
you're gonna be all over it.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:25.367
All over it.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:27.067
-Come on, bud.
-I thought it was gonna be like,

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:29.501
I get to make the only shot.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:32.200
He's perfect right?

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:35.834
They love you.
You don't have to make this.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:36.901
This is just --

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:39.300
I just appreciate you
just being here.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.067
Nothing you could do.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.567
You can shoot from up here,
whatever you feel like, Dwyane,

00:05:43.567 --> 00:05:45.467
but it's up to you, bud.

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:51.033
♪♪

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:52.367
Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:53.934
[ Sad tuba ]

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:55.767
Dude --
-I thought it was going in.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:57.067
-I'm wet.
-That was never gonna happen.

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:58.801
-I'm wet.
-That's never gonna happen.

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:00.334
That's amazing.
-My serve was too tight.

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:01.667
I couldn't go --
-You're the best, bud.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.300
Come on, you're the best.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.167
Dwyane Wade, Jack Harlow.

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:06.834
The champ!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.634
We're talking to Jack and Dwyane
after the break.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.133
Stick around, everybody!

